# Language-based routing
# /zh/* — legacy alias, no files on disk → 301 to the canonical root path
/zh/*    /:splat   301

# Every real route is a static file (zh at /, en under /en/), so no catch-all
# proxying is needed. The old "/* /index.html 200" fallback turned every bogus
# path into a 200 HTML response, which bots exploited to recurse forever
# (/skill/x/community-skills/y/assets/community-skills/…). Unknown paths now
# fall through to 404.html with a real 404 status.
#
# Note: Pages normalizes directory URLs to a trailing slash with a 308
# (/license → /license/, /skill/<slug> → /skill/<slug>/); that is expected.

# Alternate-host canonicalization (www → apex) is handled by a zone-level
# Cloudflare Redirect Rule, NOT here: Pages _redirects only matches paths,
# never hostnames. Dashboard path: h3skills.com zone → Rules → Redirect Rules.
#   www.h3skills.com/*  →  https://h3skills.com/${1}  (301, keep query string)
